From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Simon Bauer <simppabauer@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 01:19:58 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] WavStreamInstance::seek: gate the stb_vorbis path on
 WAVSTREAM_OGG

mCodec is a union, so for WAV/FLAC/MP3 streams mCodec.mOgg aliases the
dr_wav/dr_flac/dr_mp3 handle and is non-null. The bare if (mCodec.mOgg)
ran stb_vorbis_seek on a drwav struct and corrupted the native heap
(GoreGrind macOS crashes on every streamed-WAV seek and loop wrap).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HJbhV4uV7uHP6Crq1pC3di
---
 src/audiosource/wav/soloud_wavstream.cpp | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/audiosource/wav/soloud_wavstream.cpp b/src/audiosource/wav/soloud_wavstream.cpp
index 3ced545..0bc584f 100644
--- a/src/audiosource/wav/soloud_wavstream.cpp
+++ b/src/audiosource/wav/soloud_wavstream.cpp
@@ -341,7 +341,10 @@ namespace SoLoud
 
 	result WavStreamInstance::seek(double aSeconds, float* mScratch, unsigned int mScratchSize)
 	{
-		if (mCodec.mOgg)
+		// mCodec is a union: for WAV/FLAC/MP3 streams mCodec.mOgg aliases mWav/mFlac/mMp3 and is
+		// non-null, so the old bare `if (mCodec.mOgg)` ran stb_vorbis_seek on a dr_wav struct and
+		// corrupted the heap (GoreGrind macOS crashes, 2026-10-07/08). Gate on the real file type.
+		if (mParent->mFiletype == WAVSTREAM_OGG && mCodec.mOgg)
 		{
 			int pos = (int)floor(mBaseSamplerate * aSeconds);
 			stb_vorbis_seek(mCodec.mOgg, pos);
